# Game_RedGreen — Traffic Light Reflex (ID 9)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_RedGreen.h, Game_RedGreen.cpp
# HTML: data/game_redgreen_setup.html, game_redgreen_names.html, game_redgreen_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Red Light / Green Light. Groups race against cycling traffic light (RED/GREEN/YELLOW).
Press during GREEN/YELLOW = point. Press during RED = error. Time limit.

## CONFIG
- numGroups (1-10)
- speedSetting: 0=Slow(4-7s green), 1=Med(3-5s), 2=Fast(2-4s)
- timeLimit (seconds)

## STATES
RG_SETUP → RG_PREPARE (3.1s countdown) → RG_RUNNING → RG_FINISHED

## LIGHT STATES per group
TL_RED, TL_GREEN, TL_YELLOW — random durations, cycle: RED→GREEN→YELLOW→RED

## KEY MECHANICS
- 333ms debounce per puck
- Correct press (GREEN/YELLOW): score++, white flash 120ms, 50ms sound
- Wrong press (RED): red fail effect, error sequence, 1s flash
- Grace period: 150ms after light change to RED still counts as point
- Non-blocking flash reset timing
- Queued sound feedback with state-based duration (400ms RED, 100ms GREEN, 50ms other)
- 10 group colors

## COMMANDS
setup, cfg_groups, cfg_speed, cfg_time, start, stop, exit,
man_g_all, man_r_all, man_g_X, man_r_X (manual light override)

## STATUS JSON
{state, time (elapsed), limit, groups: [{id, score, light (TL enum)}]}
